# TIPPING THE VIEW OVER THE SHOULDER NEVER SNAPS (src/render/sky_light.gd,
# `horizon_share`). The air, the sky, the shadow and the light cross from the
# play camera's rules to the eye-level ones over a band of pitch; this walks the
# view down past that band with the real mouse and back up through it a degree a
# frame, at dusk, when the sun is low and every one of those rules differs most.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/shoulder-tilt.tour --seed=4 --hour=18.6 --weather=clear:0
#
# Read the frames in order: 03..14 are consecutive degrees of tilt from about 41
# down to 27 (the band is 36..28 at the shoulder's 60-degree field). Nothing
# may change between two of them except what a degree of tilt moves.
coast calm
wait 0.9
hold shoulder
await shoulder 3
wait 0.6
shot 01-level-at-dusk with shoulder,sky_in_frame
mouse 0,230 0.5
wait 0.6
shot 02-tipped-down-to-the-feet with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 03-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 04-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 05-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 06-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 07-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 08-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 09-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 10-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 11-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 12-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 13-tilt with shoulder
mouse 0,-7 0.05
wait 0.15
shot 14-tilt with shoulder
release shoulder
await top_view 3
